## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant inference design, data isolation, cost accounting, and security controls in production ML workloads on AWS.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink and API Gateway for private, authenticated access.
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint to share resources.
- Tenant-level quotas and encryption (KMS envelope keys).
- Canary releases, drift monitoring, cost attribution.

## Code Example
```javascript
function route(req){
  const payload = verifyJWT(req.headers.authorization);
  if(!payload.tenant_id) throw new Error('tenant required');
  // quota check…
  return forwardToEndpoint(payload.tenant_id, req.body);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant throttling?
- How would you audit data access across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of SageMaker for anomaly detection, focusing on real-time latency requirements, data residency constraints, and phased deployment strategies using canary releases.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection models (Isolation Forest, autoencoders)
- Time-series feature engineering (rolling windows)
- Endpoint configuration and autoscaling (min/max instances, latency targets)
- Monitoring and drift detection (SageMaker Clarify, CloudWatch)
- Cost optimization and regional data compliance

